{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/589232-is-this-how-you-would-do-the-following-feats-with-hekau","id":589232,"title":"is this how you would do the following feats with hekau?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness"],"posts":[{"date":"2015-07-13T08:27:20-07:00","id":589232,"title":"is this how you would do the following feats with hekau?","content":"1. scrying : i think combining celestial with effigy. celestial allows you to see &quot;with the sky's eyes&quot; effigy allows you to bypass physical obstacles(similar to false door)<br /> <br /> 2. making mage-like wonders. maybe combining amulets with the appropriate hekau.<br /> <br /> 3 teleportation .combining necromancy with effigies. necromancy allows with teleportation in the underworld while effigy allows you to connect objects to the underworld. essentially you are using the connection in reverse. the idea being that mummies learn about feats like teleportation indirectly. through studies of similar concepts. or an amulet of teleportation to a safe place<br /> <br /> 4. astral projection. i think alchemy will do if you stretch the concept a bit.<br /> <br /> 5. time travel. i think celestial. &quot;turning back the sky &quot; or a similar name. in that way you could propably do advanced entropy magic.<br /> <br /> 6. umbra entry. maybe necromancy? im not sure but the umbras are supposed to be connected. maybe amulets too.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1492-mark","name":"mark","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1492_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1379"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-13T21:54:15-07:00","id":589900,"title":"","content":"Its important to remember that hekau is not the same thing as mage magic. Its nowhere near as flexible, and closer to the Tremere's Thaumaturgy - a set of powers developed to mimic true magic (in this case with an ancient Egyptian theme). Because of what they are, mummies can <i>never</i> use true magic - even though many have spent millennia pursuing the secrets of Ra-hekau (true magic)<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>mark</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/589232-is-this-how-you-would-do-the-following-feats-with-hekau#post589232\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">1. scrying : i think combining celestial with effigy. celestial allows you to see &quot;with the sky's eyes&quot; effigy allows you to bypass physical obstacles(similar to false door)</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't think there is a hekau path that lets you scry. &quot;Celestial&quot; is oriented much more towards weather magic (including certain celestial phenomena like meteor showers).<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> 2. making mage-like wonders. maybe combining amulets with the appropriate hekau. </div> </div> </div>Depends on what you mean. &quot;Amulets&quot; allow a mummy to create magic talisman with pre-set effects, while &quot;Ushabti&quot; allows them to create magic statues that can come to life. And &quot;Alchemy&quot; lets them create magic potions/lotions/ointments.<br /> <br /> But again, hekau simply isn't as flexible as mage magic. Its limited to effects that an ancient Egyptian would've understood - so no magic machines or instantaneous effects.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> 3 teleportation .combining necromancy with effigies. necromancy allows with teleportation in the underworld while effigy allows you to connect objects to the underworld. essentially you are using the connection in reverse. the idea being that mummies learn about feats like teleportation indirectly. through studies of similar concepts. or an amulet of teleportation to a safe place </div> </div> </div>As far as I know, this is another power that mummies simply don't have.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> 4. astral projection. i think alchemy will do if you stretch the concept a bit. </div> </div> </div>There's a Level Four Alchemy potion called &quot;Potion of the Seperable Ka&quot; for that purpose<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> 5. time travel. i think celestial. &quot;turning back the sky &quot; or a similar name. in that way you could propably do advanced entropy magic. </div> </div> </div>Almost no one can travel in time - let alone mummies. Some mages believe that the Oracles of the Time sphere can . . .but there's limited proof of that. Others<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> 6. umbra entry. maybe necromancy? im not sure but the umbras are supposed to be connected. maybe amulets too. </div> </div> </div>Any mummy can enter the Low Umbra (i.e. the Underworld) simply by dying. For a more short-term visit, the Level One Necromancy spell &quot;Separate Ka&quot; allows the mummy to explore the Shadowlands, while the Level Three &quot;Separate Ba&quot; allows access to the Sunless Sea/Dark Kingdom/Tempest level.<br /> <br /> As for the Middle Umbra, which shapeshifters visit . . . .I don't think there is a canon hekau path. There's nothing official in the rules banning it . . . .but I doubt whether many mummies would want to experiment with it (at least on themselves). Wepauwet the werewolf was mummified, and ended up stranded in the Umbra when he tried to step sideways. <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4624-one-vorlon","name":"One Vorlon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4624_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"537"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}